re: oai n-s
part of what makes this a malicious compliance vibe is looking at *why we care about n-s in the first place*. the clay institute formalization is just an attempt at precisifying something mathematicians care about. we have good reasons to already think that n-s fails to make sense in some situations, its ontology isn't identical with that of our most fundamental theories of physics, after all. but what we care about is understanding the nature of its pathologies. where does it break down and why? and while picking apart this proof might lead us to a better understanding of that, it doesn't seem like we have at present gained such an understanding from OAI's paper nor its lean cert. there is still a lot left to wonder about, with the failure of N-S, even now that we have a lean-certified proof that there exists a very unphysical setup that apparently nobody really understands which blows up. questions remain such as: is there any *physically realizable, or nearly so* setup which induces a blowup? what aspects of the setup openai published are actually important? are there other ways to go about it?

